.git
.gitignore
.cline
.env
.env.*
.venv
venv
node_modules

# Local runtime state and secrets must never enter build contexts.
.velox
DataServer/.velox
DataServer/data

# Live worker-certification runtime artifacts (root-owned, 0600: rendered MP4s,
# pass_criteria/recovery JSON) must never enter build contexts. The images only
# need RemoteCodex/.../tests/fixtures/engine_selftest_baseline.sha256.
tests/worker-cert

# Local build outputs are not Docker inputs.
DataServer/bin
RemoteCodex/native/worker-agent-go/bin
RemoteCodex/native/video-engine-cpp/build*

# Generic transient files.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.log

# Large local media and generated build evidence are never Docker inputs.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mkv
*.webm
**/tmp
**/output
# Keep DataServer/internal/artifacts in the server build context: it is a
# compiled Go package, not generated output. Exclude only generated artifact
# directories outside the source tree.
artifacts
**/output/artifacts
**/coverage
docs/benchmarks/evidence

# CI/deployment metadata is not needed by either production image.
.github
docs
ops
deploy
DataServer/data/ansible

# Go test sources are compile-time-only inputs and are never shipped.
#
# Safety review (why this cannot break a build):
#   * No Dockerfile or compose in this repo runs `go test` / `go vet`. The
#     only test runner inside any image is `ctest` in the worker's
#     cpp-builder stage, and its inputs are `*_test.cpp` (video-engine-cpp/
#     tests/), which this pattern does NOT match — C++ test sources stay.
#   * `go build` ignores `*_test.go` by definition, so the master
#     (cmd/server), the worker (agent/evict/benchmark-tools) and
#     Dockerfile.chronon (agent) are unaffected.
#   * The only production `//go:embed` directive is
#     shared/telemetry/catalog_source.go -> schema/catalog.json (not a _test
#     file). Every other `//go:embed` lives inside a `_test.go` file, so it
#     is already dropped together with its own file.
#   * `*_test.go` does NOT match the C++ engine tests (`*_test.cpp`), nor the
#     `tests/fixtures/engine_selftest_baseline.sha256` fixture that the worker
#     runtime stage explicitly COPYs. Do NOT widen this to `**/tests/`.
**/*_test.go
